+
+Version **0.1.8** adds **⋮ → Delete chat** in Workspace project cards and the chat toolbar, with confirmation. It deletes conversation records/messages/citations/tool history transactionally while keeping the project, files, memory and models. Open-chat deletion stops generation and unloads native session state before returning to Workspace. Reopening starts an empty chat. Room stays schema 2; install as an update without clearing app data. [Behavior and phone checks](docs/CHAT_DELETION_018.md).
+
+[Download the signed 0.1.8 ARM64 APK from Drive](https://drive.google.com/file/d/1odrfBn_RHILGYj7Gvm8H6sPqVcfk10b3/view?usp=drivesdk): 91,387,833 bytes, versionCode9, same update certificate. Current validation:104 app tests executed/PASS,2 unchanged LiteRT compatibility tests up to date; debug/release assembly PASS; lint0errors/73existing warnings. Native library SHA-256 values match the verified0.1.7 manifest. Local distribution APKs now use `dist/apk`, outside Gradle's automatically cleaned packaging directory. [Artifact manifest](docs/validation/apk-018.json).
+
+The following runtime quality findings and timings belong to the preceding 0.1.7 investigation; this chat-management update does not claim a model-quality or performance fix.
 
 Latest supplied Qwen CPU captures show consecutive completed turns and metrics behind Details, but the communes question receives unrelated categories: **answer relevance FAIL**. Its installed version/hash/context/timings are not shown. Earlier physical metrics remain first visible text3.338s, 85 output tokens in25.290s at3.55tokens/s with healthy engine/session reuse. Version **0.1.7** moves benchmarks into Details, starts real model preparation at chat entry, exposes measured output cuts and provides real Continue generation. It retains the0.1.6 template-role/history/reuse fixes. Room remains schema2 and private models/chats are preserved. See [implementation/latency](docs/CHAT_LATENCY_AND_OUTPUT_017.md) and [the new relevance audit](docs/LITERT_RELEVANCE_AUDIT_017.md).
 
